      'His insistence, once finally summoned before the king, on having his name formally cleared before accepting freedom shows that a wrongly accused person is entitled to full vindication, not merely quiet release.',
      'His complete, unforced forgiveness of the very brothers who tried to erase him — "No blame will there be upon you today" — offered from a position of total power over their fate, stands as one of the Quran\'s clearest models of forgiveness extended precisely when vengeance would have been easiest.',
